{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the children of Israel.</b> Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] explained that He saw the oppression that the Egyptians were doing to them openly; <b>and Elohim knew</b> — what was done to them in secret. And Rashi explained <b>and Elohim knew</b>: He set His heart upon them and did not hide His eye from them. And this is correct according to the plain sense, for at first He had been hiding His face from them, and it was for eating, but now Elohim heard their groaning and saw them, to say that He no longer hid His face from them, and He knew their pain and all that was done to them and all that they needed. And Scripture lengthened to mention many claims on behalf of their redemption: 'And Elohim heard their groaning,' 'And Elohim remembered His covenant,' 'And Elohim saw,' 'And Elohim knew,' 'For I know his pain' (Exodus 3:7) — for even though the time decreed upon them had been completed, they were not worthy of being redeemed, as is explained by Ezekiel (Ezekiel 20:8), but rather because of the outcry He accepted their prayer in His mercy. And by way of truth, this verse contains a great secret from the mysteries of the Torah, to say that their suffering ascended before the light of His face and drew them near to the Da'at, as it is said, 'In the midst of years make it known, in wrath remember mercy' (Habakkuk 3:2), and therefore Scripture lengthens in this matter after it already said 'And Elohim heard,' 'And Elohim remembered.' And this verse is explained in the midrash of Rabbi Nechunya ben HaKanah (Sefer HaBahir §136); you will understand it from there."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase 'and it was for eating' (והיה לאכל) is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. 'The light of His face' translates מאור פניו, meaning the luminary of the countenance, a kabbalistic term left cryptic per the way of truth. The verse citation from Sefer HaBahir is given as אות עו in the source, resolved here as §136 by standard numeration (ע=70, ו=6)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:01:22.656512239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}